+# Incidents brief, August–September 2026
+
+Follow-up status as of the 30 September meeting.
+
+## 11 August: ingest stalled, database disk full
+
+- **Impact:** About two and a half hours overnight without new data; customers saw stale dashboards. No data lost.
+- **Cause:** A malformed batch jammed the ingest service in endless retries, whose logs filled the database disk until it refused writes.
+- **Fix:** Restarted ingest with the bad batch set aside; reclaimed database space and cleared old logs.
+- **Follow-ups:**
+  - Disk alert at 80% (Sunil): done.
+  - Stop bad batches jamming ingest (Jonas): open, in review.
+  - Faster paging escalation (Elif): done.
+
+## 21 September: API down, expired certificate
+
+- **Impact:** 47 minutes on a Monday morning when browsers and nearly all customer systems could not reach the API.
+- **Cause:** The API's certificate expired; automatic renewal had failed silently all month on an outdated access key.
+- **Fix:** Renewed the certificate and restarted the API; the repaired renewal job now alerts on failure.
+- **Follow-ups:**
+  - Reminder 14 days before expiry (Priya): done.
+  - Alert on days left (Priya): open.
+  - Expiry check in weekly checklist (Tomasz): open.
+  - Responders note steps during incidents (Mara): done.
